    "message": "Let default generated Scenarios start and use their toilets\n\nDefault Web drafts were never startable: every draft stopped on the\nguardian blocker and, below about 1,000 m², on the accessible-route\nblocker. Separately, nobody in a generated Scenario ever reached a\ntoilet, because Agents started knowing no facilities and only learned\none by arriving at it.\n\n- Standard plan: widen rooms narrower than the 1.8 m accessible doorway,\n  taking the area from the sleeping zone; grow the default area until\n  the sleeping zone still holds everyone at 3.5 m² per person.\n- Population: when no household composition is entered, use assumed\n  synthetic templates that link each generated minor to an adult in\n  the same household (new \"assumption\" composition source kind).\n- Agent dynamics v2, selected by model_configs.agent_dynamics: Agents\n  know the shared service facilities from the start. Scenarios without\n  the config keep v1, so saved histories replay unchanged.\n\nThe three assumptions are recorded in provenance, the source manifest\nand docs/simulation-models.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
